# Streamlit UI, worker, replay

Three screens in `app.py`: **Data**, **Train**, **Test & Replay**. English copy. Stock Streamlit theme + Plotly. Bind `127.0.0.1:8501`; telemetry off (`.streamlit/config.toml`).

**Worker:** prepare/train via `spawn_worker` → `python -m pdm.worker`. One heavy job. Status atomic JSON under `runs/_worker/`. UI polls (`st.fragment`); page rerun must not spawn a second job. `Stop` sets `stop.flag` only — do not kill unrelated PIDs.

Statuses: `not_ready`, `preparing`, `ready`, `training`, `completed`, `stopped`, `failed`. No data → say so, do not fake results.

**Replay isolation** (`replay.py`):
```text
ReplaySource (rows ≤ t) → Predictor → AlertEngine
Evaluator joins actual RUL afterwards; never as model input
```
`Show ground truth` must not change predictions. Issued forecasts are append-only. `Reset` starts a new replay.

**Alerts (`AlertEngine`):** warn when predicted RUL ≤ H for K consecutive steps; reset when RUL > 1.2H for K steps. Early windows: `Collecting history` (no future padding).

**Plots:** separate axes — do not overlay pressure and RUL. Bearings: RMS. Filters: Δp with 600 Pa line. CSV export of predictions/alerts required.

CLI: `doctor`, `download`, `inspect`, `prepare`, `train`, `evaluate`, `app`, `stop`.
